From: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: sfp: keep SFP-10G-T as optical SR (rollball PHY handled by 4003)

The unbranded "OEM SFP-10G-T" 10GBASE-T copper SFP+ module advertises
SFP-MSA transceiver code 0x10 (10GBASE-SR fiber) in its EEPROM byte 3.
The existing kernel quirk

  SFP_QUIRK_F("OEM", "SFP-10G-T", sfp_fixup_rollball_cc)

correctly sets sfp->mdio_protocol = MDIO_I2C_ROLLBALL so the PHY probe
path can access the RTL8261 PHY behind the Rollball MDIO bridge. The PHY
probe itself fails with -EINVAL on FMan memac with managed="in-band-status"
(handled non-fatally by patch 101/4003 — "PHY probe returned -22,
continuing without PHY").

The module MUST be kept as optical SR (connector unchanged) so that
phylink_sfp_config_optical() finds a common interface (10GBASER in both
the SFP and MAC interface bitmaps). Changing the connector to RJ45
(via sfp_fixup_fs_10gt) causes sfp_parse_support() to clear the
10GBASER interface, making the optical-path intersection empty and
producing "unsupported SFP module: no common interface modes".

After the non-fatal PHY probe fallback, the MAC's 10GBASE-R in-band
sync detects carrier once the RTL8261 PHY completes copper auto-neg
with the link partner. This is the same path used by genuine SFP-10G-SR
modules.

Patch 4003/101 (sfp-rollball-phylink-fallback) is a prerequisite —
without it the -EINVAL is fatal and the module enters SFP_S_FAIL state.

Verified on hardware 2026-06-21 (LS1046A Mono Gateway, kernel 6.18.34-vyos,
nxp-ask branch, FMan memac 1af0000 / eth4).

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -579,7 +579,15 @@ static const struct sfp_quirk sfp_quirks[] = {
 	// OEM SFP-GE-T is a 1000Base-T module with broken TX_FAULT indicator
 	SFP_QUIRK_F("OEM", "SFP-GE-T", sfp_fixup_ignore_tx_fault),

-	SFP_QUIRK_F("OEM", "SFP-10G-T", sfp_fixup_rollball_cc),
+	// OEM SFP-10G-T is a 10GBASE-T copper rollball module that
+	// advertises 10GBASE-SR fiber transceiver codes (byte 3 = 0x10)
+	// in its EEPROM. Keep the module as optical SR so the phylink
+	// optical config path finds a common 10GBASER interface. The
+	// rollball PHY probe failure (-EINVAL on in-band FMan memac)
+	// is handled non-fatally by patch 101/4003. After falling
+	// through, the MAC's 10GBASE-R in-band sync detects carrier
+	// once the RTL8261 PHY completes copper auto-negotiation.
+	SFP_QUIRK_F("OEM", "SFP-10G-T", sfp_fixup_rollball_cc),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-T", sfp_quirk_oem_2_5g),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-BX10-D", sfp_quirk_2500basex),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-BX10-U", sfp_quirk_2500basex),
